## Regulatory Rate Review Framework and URRT Single Risk Pool Evaluation

Rate submissions for ACA-compliant individual and small group plans in Pennsylvania are governed by [45 CFR § 154.215(a)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/section-154.215) and annual guidance issued by the Pennsylvania Insurance Department. Issuers are required to submit rate filings electronically via the System for Electronic Rates and Forms Filing (SERFF), incorporating the federal Unified Rate Review Template (URRT), an actuarial memorandum, and detailed plan benefit descriptions. The filing mandate applies to all ACA-compliant plans offered both on the Pennie exchange and off-exchange, regardless of whether the proposed filing reflects a rate increase, rate decrease, or unchanged premium structure.

Under [45 CFR § 156.80](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/section-156.80), issuers must establish a "single risk pool" that includes all enrollees in all non-grandfathered individual or small group health plans offered by the issuer in the state. The single risk pool baseline is established using historical experience period allowed claims, adjusted for run-out, incurred but not reported (IBNR) claims, and expected risk adjustment transfers. Actuaries project this baseline forward to the PY 2027 rating period using annual claim trends categorized into unit cost inflation and service utilization components.

