## CMS Plan ID Crosswalk Mapping and Passive Re-Enrollment Protocol

To preserve coverage continuity for consumers who do not actively select a plan during the annual Open Enrollment Period (OEP), CMS and the Pennsylvania Insurance Department enforce standardized auto-enrollment crosswalk rules. The Plan ID Crosswalk framework maps prior-year Qualified Health Plan (QHP) Plan IDs and service area combinations to upcoming Plan Year Plan IDs. The auto-re-enrollment process is governed by statutory standards set forth in [45 CFR § 155.335(j)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/section-155.335), which establish a strict hierarchy for crosswalking enrollees from discontinued or modified plans into available coverage.

Issuers submitting QHP applications in Pennsylvania must execute their Plan ID Crosswalk Templates within the Marketplace Plan Management System (MPMS) Module in HIOS or SERFF. For PY 2027, the initial submission window deadline was set for June 10, 2026, with the final issuer plan confirmation and crosswalk deadline established as August 31, 2026. Issuers are legally required to secure explicit state approval via the Plan ID Crosswalk State Authorization Form or formal PDF authorization from the Pennsylvania Insurance Department prior to CMS finalizing auto-enrollment transactions.

The statutory re-enrollment mapping hierarchy under [45 CFR § 155.335(j)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/section-155.335) follows a strict multi-tier progression to safeguard member plan continuity:

1. **Plan retained:** If a plan continues to be offered in the same service area, the enrollee is mapped directly to the same 14-digit Plan ID.
2. **Plan modified:** If an issuer discontinues a plan, it must crosswalk the enrollee to a plan within the same product structure, same actuarial value metal tier, and identical provider network ID.
3. **Modified network:** If no plan with the same network ID exists, the enrollee is mapped to a plan within the same product and metal tier under a modified network ID.
4. **Adjacent metal tier:** If no plan in the same metal tier is available within the product, the issuer must map the enrollee to a plan one metal level higher or lower than the discontinued plan.
5. **Alternative product:** If the entire product structure is discontinued, the issuer may crosswalk enrollees to an alternative product structure offered by the same issuer that matches the metal tier.
6. **Market exit:** If an issuer completely exits a rating area or market, enrollees may be crosswalked to an alternative carrier's plan if authorized by Pennie and CMS under state-approved market-exit protocols.

